The macOS build links Apple's libc++ and system frameworks dynamically
(VideoToolbox and AudioToolbox among them); none of them are
distributed. The Linux build needs only glibc, and the Windows build
links only Windows system DLLs, including the Direct3D 11 and 12 and
DXVA2 interfaces used by the D3D11VA, D3D12VA and DXVA2 hardware paths.

